==Trivia==
*The first use of rockets were in 1232, when reports appeared describing fire arrows and 'iron pots' that could be heard for 25 kilometers when they exploded upon impact, causing devastation for a radius of 600 meters, apparently due to shrapnel. A "flying fire-lance" that had reusable barrels was also mentioned to have been used by the Jin dynasty. Rockets are recorded to have been used by the Song navy in a military exercise dated to 1245. Rockets are still used to this day for multiple purposes, whether that is military, science, and entertainment.
**The Rocket is 1 of 5 [[cards]] associated with rocketry, with the others being [[Firecracker]], [[Goblin Machine]], [[Party Rocket]], and [[Rocket Silo]].
**A Trainer in the [[Training Camp]] is called Trainer Rocket and uses a rocketry-related card in the [[Battle Decks|deck]], which is Rocket.
**Its hull looks similar to the barrel of the [[Skeleton Barrel]], [[Goblin Demolisher]], [[Balloon]], and [[Goblin Barrel]].
*While not available as a spell in Clash of Clans, the Rocket reappears there in a few situations.
**2 Rockets can be seen attached on both sides of the [https://clashofclans.fandom.com/wiki/Rocket_Balloon Rocket Balloon's] hot air balloon.
**In the [https://clashofclans.fandom.com/wiki/Scenery?file=Map_10th_Clashiversary.jpg 10th Clashiversary Scenery], the [https://clashofclans.fandom.com/wiki/Scenery?file=10th_Clashiversary_Scenery_Boat.png Boat] is reskinned as a balloon with 2 Rockets attached on both sides of its hot air balloon, like the Rocket Balloon.
**The Rocket is used from the [https://clashofclans.fandom.com/wiki/Rocket_Artillery Rocket Artillery], a defensive building in the [https://clashofclans.fandom.com/wiki/Clan_Capital Clan Capital].
*The Rocket is tied with [[Lightning]] for the most expensive [[:Category:Spell Cards|spell]], costing 6 [[Elixir]], excluding the [[Mirror]] as it does not have a [[:Category:Variable-Elixir Cards|defined Elixir cost]].
*The Rocket deals the highest damage out of all spells, with 2,163 damage at Level 15.
*The Rocket is one of the first spell cards to be featured in a Trainer's deck, alongside the [[Arrows]], [[Zap]], and [[Fireball]].
*The Rocket is one of the first spells to be featured in a [[Loading Screens|Loading Screen]], alongside the Arrows and Fireball.
*The Rocket is one of the first spell cards to receive a card render, alongside the Arrows and [[Barbarian Barrel]].
*Its [[Star Points|Star Level 3 Skin]] has a [[Goblins|Goblin]] riding on top of it.
*The [[Baby Goblins]] are responsible for creating the Rocket, according to the Clash Royale [https://youtube.com/shorts/9_N_r0Nib2c?si=JDSgvKgJbdPfJiPe Goblin Machine Lore Drop video].
*The Rocket is unavailable in multiple [[Tournament/Special Event Challenges|special gamemodes]]. More specifically:
**It is 1 of 3 cards that is unavailable in Timeless Towers, the others being [[Goblin Drill]] and Miner.
**It is 1 of 12 cards that is unavailable in [[Chess Royale]], the others being [[Royal Recruits]], [[Earthquake]], Lightning, [[Poison]], Goblin Drill, Miner, [[Golden Knight]], [[Skeleton King]], [[Archer Queen]], [[Mighty Miner]], and the [[Monk]].
*The Rocket is the subject of certain cosmetics in the game. More specifically:
**The Rocket is the subject of a few [[Clans|Clan]] badges.
**The Rocket is the subject of an [[Emotes|Emote]]. 
***It is also 1 of 3 cards in which an Emote it is the subject of relates to one of its Star Levels, the others being the [[Elite Barbarians]] and [[Hog Rider]].
*The Rocket was featured in the winning deck of the [https://www.youtube.com/live/psZXKWHkKkE?si=PbjvbZt8stghz6eJ King's Cup II Tournament], by a player called Surgical Goblin.
*Before the Rocket's card release, the Rocket's damage was increased by 7%.

